wlanpi-mcp (0.3.4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Align tooling and packaging with the WLAN-Pi organization standard,
    using wlanpi-core as the reference. Adopt a Python 3.13-only floor:
    requires-python is now >=3.13, the 3.11/3.12 classifiers are replaced
    with a single 3.13 classifier, and debian/control Build-Depends,
    X-Python3-Version, and Pre-Depends all require python3 (>= 3.13).
  * Add the six org-standard GitHub Actions workflows under
    .github/workflows/: test-python-package (tox on a 3.13 matrix),
    python-format-police (tox -e formatcheck), python-lint-police
    (tox -e lint), codeql-analysis, build-and-archive-debian-package and
    deploy-to-packagecloud (both via the reusable WLAN-Pi/gh-workflows
    sbuild + packagecloud pipeline).
  * Add .github/dependabot.yml (weekly pip updates scoped to the runtime
    dependencies) and a tox.ini providing the test, lint, format,
    formatcheck, and flake8 environments with the autoflake/black/isort/
    flake8 toolchain, plus scripts/check_whitespace.sh and
    scripts/fix_whitespace.sh.
  * Add [tool.black] (py313 target) and [tool.isort] (black profile) to
    pyproject.toml.

